.TH PUMAS 1 "2026-08-20" "pumas 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pumas \- power usage monitor for Apple Silicon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pumas
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pumas
is a power usage monitor for Apple Silicon Macs. It displays CPU, GPU, ANE,
memory, frequency, and package power metrics collected from macOS utilities.
.PP
The
.B run
command requires
.BR sudo
because macOS's
.B powermetrics
utility requires root access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the power usage monitor.
.TP
.B generate-completion
Print a shell completion script to stdout. Requires a shell argument such as
.BR bash ,
.BR fish ,
.BR powershell ,
.BR elvish , or
.BR zsh .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \\-h ", " \\-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \\-V ", " \\-\-version
Print version.
.SH RUN OPTIONS
Options for the
.B run
command.
.TP
.BI \\-i " SAMPLE_RATE_MS" ", " \\-\-sample-rate " SAMPLE_RATE_MS"
Update rate in milliseconds. The minimum is 100; the default is 1000.
PowerMetrics samples at this rate.
.TP
.BI \\-\-history-size " HISTORY_SIZE"
Number of recent samples to keep in history for each metric. The default is
128.
.TP
.BI \\-\-accent-color " COLOR"
ANSI color code for labels. The default is 2 (green).
.TP
.BI \\-\-gauge-fg-color " COLOR"
ANSI color code for the gauge foreground. The default is 2 (green).
.TP
.BI \\-\-gauge-bg-color " COLOR"
ANSI color code for the gauge background. The default is 7 (white).
.TP
.BI \\-\-history-fg-color " COLOR"
ANSI color code for history graphs. The default is 4 (blue).
.TP
.BI \\-\-history-bg-color " COLOR"
ANSI color code for history graph backgrounds. The default is 7 (white).
.TP
.BR \\-\-json
Print metrics to stdout as newline-delimited JSON instead of running the UI.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the interactive monitor:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pumas run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream metrics and select a value with
.BR jq :
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo pumas run --json | jq '.metrics.e_clusters[0].cpus[2].active_ratio'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate completions for Zsh:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pumas generate-completion zsh > _pumas
.fi
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
Use the arrow keys to switch between tabs. Press
.BR Esc ,
.BR q ,
.BR x , or
.B Ctrl-C
 to quit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred while parsing arguments, collecting metrics, or running the
monitor.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I schema/schema.json
JSON schema for export mode.
.TP
.I schema/sample-output.json
Example output for export mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powermetrics (1),
.BR jq (1)
.SH AUTHORS
graelo <https://github.com/graelo/pumas>
